Feature profile from 30 known actives (conserved = present in at least 80%):
  aromatic_ring: 100% of actives, 98% of background (1.0x)  <- prevalent but not discriminating
  basic_nitrogen_any: 97% of actives, 53% of background (1.8x)  <- conserved
  halogen_on_aromatic: 93% of actives, 33% of background (2.8x)  <- conserved
  amidine: 90% of actives, 4% of background (22.5x)  <- conserved
  primary_aliphatic_amine: 90% of actives, 17% of background (5.4x)  <- conserved
  amide: 77% of actives, 28% of background (2.8x)
  aminopyridine: 70% of actives, 17% of background (4.1x)
  guanidine: 30% of actives, 1% of background (32.7x)
  secondary_alcohol: 10% of actives, 15% of background (0.7x)
  hydroxyethylene: 10% of actives, 10% of background (1.0x)
  secondary_aliphatic_amine: 7% of actives, 14% of background (0.5x)
  nitrile: 7% of actives, 8% of background (0.9x)
  Set aside as ubiquitous: aromatic_ring. Prevalent among the actives and no rarer elsewhere, so their presence in a candidate says nothing about binding.

